    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on exploiting high-ceiling speed profiles against favorable defensive matchups, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (74.65) and **Seiya Suzuki** (72.23). **Corbin Carroll** is our primary engine today; while facing Kevin Gausman presents a moderate challenge, the aggressive baserunning potential against a slow-working starter pushes his value well into the elite tier. Similarly, **Seiya Suzuki** benefits from a stellar projection against Merrill Kelly, whose 5.27 xERA creates a perfect storm for run production at the top of our order. While **Mickey Moniak** (60.19) and **Max Muncy** (61.65) round out our high-floor starters, keep a close watch on **Max Muncy**, who benefits from a specific matchup quirk\u2014a slow pitcher delivery that signals a higher likelihood of productive counts and potential stolen base opportunities.\n\nThe margins were tight for our utility slots, and **Cole Young** was the closest to breaking into the starting nine. Ultimately, **Cole Young**\u2019s score of 31.76 was anchored by a brutal matchup against Zack Wheeler; the combination of an elite arm and a lower spot in the batting order dropped him well below our 40-point efficiency floor. **Josh Naylor** (47.91) remains in the lineup despite the tough Wheeler assignment, as his current lineup protection outweighs the risks associated with **Cole Young**. We are monitoring the status of **Gabriel Moreno**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Max Muncy**, **Seiya Suzuki**, and **Corbin Carroll** closely as their lineups remain pending; any shift to the bottom of the order could necessitate a re-evaluation of their daily efficiency scores.\n\nAs we navigate the tail end of August, we are forced to manage our game caps carefully, leading to the benching of **Jose Caballero** and **Brice Turang** due to off-days, while **Trevor Story** remains sidelined on the IL. While we maintain roster depth with players like **James Wood**, **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte**, today\u2019s board dictates that **Zach McKinstry** (40.86) gets the nod for his park-adjusted upside. Be advised that **Zach McKinstry** is near our substitution threshold; if weather trends or late-scratch reports shift, we have the flexibility to adjust.",
